Tenali Rama and the Heavy Pumpkin (Raw Story)

One day, King Krishnadevaraya wanted to test the wisdom of his courtiers.

He gave each of them a pumpkin and said, “Fill this pumpkin with the wisest thing you can find.”

All the courtiers were confused. Some filled it with gold, others with jewels, thinking they were valuable.

Tenali Rama quietly took his pumpkin home.

He made a small hole in it and carefully filled it with curd.

After that, he sealed the hole so it looked untouched.

The next day, everyone brought their pumpkins to the king.

The king checked each one, but he was not impressed.

When it was Tenali’s turn, the king opened the pumpkin and found it filled with curd.

Tenali smiled and said, “Your Majesty, curd represents knowledge. Just like curd forms from milk, wisdom grows from learning.”

The king was pleased with his answer.

He declared Tenali Rama the wisest among them.

💖 Moral:

True wisdom comes from knowledge, not wealth.
